<title>HUNGARY: Overall gains push CESI index higher.</title>
<headline>Overall gains push CESI index higher.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The CESI Central European Share Index rose on Monday to close at 1,517.09 points, up 8.32 points or 0.55 percent, the Budapest Stock Stock Exchange said on its Reuters page.</p>
<p>The index advanced as all the three markets closed higher.</p>
<p>The index, which has been published since February 1, reflects the trend of 50 shares on the Budapest, Prague and Warsaw bourses.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 266 2410</p>
